==English==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|en|scientific|ally}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-us-scientifically.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# Using science or methods of science.
# Using the [[scientific method]].
# [[methodically|Methodically]].
#: ''He tried to approach his bad habits '''scientifically'''.''
# With regard to [[science]].
# From a scientific perspective.
#: '''''Scientifically''', there's nothing special about the year 2012.''
#* {{RQ:Conrad Heart of Darkness|page=210|passage=I remembered the old doctor, - ‘It would be interesting for science to watch the mental changes of individuals, on the spot.’ I felt I was becoming '''scientifically''' interesting.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|methodically}} {{l|en|systematically}}, {{l|en|systemwise}}; see also [[Thesaurus:methodically]]

